Grayswandir's stronger - but mainly because it does silver damage
against major demons. Other than that, it's pretty much on par with a
lawfully-wielded Sceptre.

Even if you don't want to wield the Sceptre, carrying it can be useful
- it can be #invoked for hunger-free ringless conflict.

The sceptre has two weak spots: it's pretty weak against hostile
lawfuls, and it can be stolen by the Wizard of Yendor, which would
result in a disarmed character facing a death-ray-immune Rodney.

